WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.790
Everyone who's anyone in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe showed up for the final fight in

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.620
Avengers: Endgame including one character
you most likely didn't spot.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.860
Several eagle-eyed fans discovered that none
other than Howard the Duck makes a cameo appearance

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.490
during Endgame's climax.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.420
"No one laughs at a master of quack fu!"

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.760
Well, not exactly THAT one.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:21.980
This one.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.580
The anthropomorphic duck pops up after Doctor
Strange, Wong, and dozens of other mystic

00:00:26.599 --> 00:00:31.609
sorcerers open up portals for the heroes who
were dusted in Avengers: Endgame to step through

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:36.350
and join the battle against Thanos, his sinister
Black Order minions, his alien army, and his

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.220
massive ship.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.660
Howard isn't easily located in Endgame's final
fight if you don't know where to look for

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.160
him.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.800
Right as Hope van Dyne steps into frame, Howard
can be seen on the lower-right side of the

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.850
screen, passing through the portal as part
of a group that includes several members of

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:55.269
the Guardians of the Galaxy series' Ravagers,
coming to Earth to settle an interstellar

00:00:55.269 --> 00:00:56.480
score with Thanos.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.320
If you blink, you'll miss him and a lot of
people did.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:04.180
Howard's cameo in Avengers: Endgame raises
a big question: Was he among the people decimated

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.960
when Thanos snapped his fingers at the end
of Infinity War?

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.060
Or did he manage to survive the Mad Titan's
mass-murder?

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:14.080
Apparently, Howard the Duck was one of the
lucky individuals in the universe who were

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.920
spared, with Joe and Anthony Russo confirming
to The Huffington Post that, quote, "he survived."

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.040
Created by writer Steve Gerber and artist
Val Mayerik, Howard the Duck is a self-styled

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.460
master of martial arts who has an undefined
grasp on magic.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.350
Despite those limited abilities he claims
to possess, as well as the frequency with

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:36.920
which he's pal'd around with Marvel's mightiest,
he's rarely shown as possessing any typical

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.040
superhero powers.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.880
This is different when he suits up as the
Iron Duck, gaining superhuman durability and

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.440
strength, as well as a flamethrower on each
arm.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:50.530
However, Howard is just Howard in Endgame
so we can't say for certain how helpful he

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:51.620
might have been in the fight.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.320
Fans first saw Howard in the MCU in 2014's
Guardians of the Galaxy, in which he appeared

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:02.220
as a living part of the Collector's museum,
alongside fellow easter egg Cosmo the Spacedog.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.120
"What do you let it lick you like that for?

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:11.540
Gross."

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.689
Seth Green provided the voice for the CGI
character, then again lent his voice to Howard

00:02:16.689 --> 00:02:19.700
for 2017's Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:24.980
In that film, Howard was seen having yet another
drink — this time on the icy planet Contraxia

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.360
while flirting with a woman.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.160
"You know what they say — you're out of
luck until you've gone duck!"

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.860
These appearances in the Guardians franchise
were reportedly intended to lead to a part

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.660
for Howard the Duck in Infinity War.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:40.020
But sadly, the cameo never happened.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.560
Speaking in an interview with Fandom, Anthony
Russo explained,

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.000
"Howard the Duck was in one draft of the script.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.420
Howard the Duck actually had a really good
scene.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.080
[...] We were going to cameo Ken Jeong, with
Howard the Duck.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.200
That was a much-beloved scene by us but it
just didn't end up fitting at all."

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.720
According to Joe Russo,

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.660
"[The scene involved Peter] Quill trying to
track down some information from Howard the

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:04.460
Duck on some outlier planet and interrupting
him during a poker game."

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.180
Though neither Howard the Duck nor Ken Jeong
made it to Infinity War, they both had some

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.500
screen time in Endgame.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:15.180
Howard showed up at the tail end of the movie,
while Jeong made a cameo early on, playing

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.320
the security guard who helped Scott Lang get
out of the storage facility in San Francisco.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:23.760
For a while now, there have been whisperings
of the possibility of a new Howard the Duck

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:29.340
movie, which would mark the second film based
on the wise-cracking duck after his 1986 debut.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:35.390
Back in 2017, Marvel Studios president Kevin
Feige teased a future for Howard in the MCU,

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:36.260
saying,

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.099
"You know, the fun thing about Howard is he
shows up where you least expect him.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.000
[...] Who knows where he's going to appear
next?"

